"2748","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 2748 Arabic Hadees: 1286"
"2749","On the authority of Abu Hurairah and Abu Sa'id, who both bore witness that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""When the servant says, 'There is no god but Allah, and Allah is the Greatest,' Allah the Mighty and Majestic says: 'My servant has spoken the truth: There is no god but Me, and I am the Greatest.' And when the servant says: 'There is no god but Allah alone,' He says: 'My servant has spoken the truth: There is no god but Me alone.' And when he says: 'There is no god but Allah, He has no partner,' He says: 'My servant has spoken the truth: There is no god but Me, and I have no partner.' And when he says: 'There is no god but Allah, to Him belongs the dominion and to Him belongs all praise,' He says: 'My servant has spoken the truth: There is no god but Me, to Me belongs the dominion and to Me belongs all praise.' And when he says: 'There is no god but Allah, and there is no power and no strength except with Allah,' He says: 'My servant has spoken the truth: There is no god but Me, and there is no power and no strength except with Me.' Whoever is granted these words at the time of his death, the Fire will not touch him."""""
