"2780","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 2780 Arabic Hadees: 1795"
"2781","Shall I not tell you of something which, if you adhere to it, you will catch up with those who have surpassed you, and no one will surpass you after it, and you will be the best among those around you, except for one who does the same as you? You glorify Allah (say Subḥān Allāh), praise Him (say Al-ḥamdu lillāh), and magnify Him (say Allāhu Akbar) thirty-three times after every prayer.On the authority of Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The poor came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: ""The people of wealth have taken the highest degrees and lasting bliss. They pray as we pray, and fast as we fast, but they have surplus wealth with which they perform Hajj and ʿUmrah, strive in the cause of Allah, and give charity."" He said: ... and he mentioned it (the narration).We differed among ourselves, so some of us said: ""We glorify thirty-three times, praise thirty-three times, and magnify thirty-four times."" So I returned to him and he said: ""You say: Subḥān Allāh, Al-ḥamdu lillāh, Allāhu Akbar, until each of them reaches thirty-three."""""
