"2795","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 2795 Arabic Hadees: 1461"
"2796","On the authority of Aisha, that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) taught her this supplication: ""O Allah, I ask You for all good, its immediate and its deferred, what I know of it and what I do not know. And I seek refuge in You from all evil, its immediate and its deferred, what I know of it and what I do not know. O Allah, I ask You for the good that Your servant and Prophet asked You for, and I seek refuge in You from the evil that Your servant and Prophet sought refuge in You from. O Allah, I ask You for Paradise and that which brings one closer to it of word or deed, and I seek refuge in You from the Fire and that which brings one closer to it of word or deed. And I ask You to make every decree You have decreed for me good."""""
