"2871","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 2871 Arabic Hadees: 893"
"2872","Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) reported: A Bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: ""O Messenger of Allah, teach me something good."" The Prophet ﷺ took him by the hand and said: ""Say: Subḥānallāh (Glory be to Allah), wal-ḥamdu lillāh (All praise is due to Allah), wa lā ilāha illallāh (There is no deity but Allah), wallāhu akbar (Allah is the Greatest)."" The Bedouin counted them on his fingers and left. After a while, he returned, and the Prophet ﷺ smiled. He said: ""The poor man reflected."" He came and said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Subḥānallāh, wal-ḥamdu lillāh, wa lā ilāha illallāh, wallāhu akbar — this is for Allah; so what is for me?"" The Prophet ﷺ said to him: ""O Bedouin! When you say: Subḥānallāh, Allah says: 'You have spoken the truth.' When you say: Al-ḥamdu lillāh, Allah says: 'You have spoken the truth.' When you say: Lā ilāha illallāh, Allah says: 'You have spoken the truth.' When you say: Allāhu akbar, Allah says: 'You have spoken the truth.' When you say: Allāhumma ighfir lī (O Allah, forgive me), Allah says: 'I have done so.' When you say: Allāhumma arḥimnī (O Allah, have mercy on me), Allah says: 'I have done so.' When you say: Allāhumma arzuqnī (O Allah, provide for me), Allah says: 'I have done so.'"" The Bedouin then counted seven on his fingers and departed."
"2873","Abu al-Tayyah narrated: I said to Abd al-Rahman ibn Khabbash al-Tamimi, who was a very old man: ""Did you meet the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?"" He said: ""Yes."" I said: ""How did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ deal with the night when the devils nearly overwhelmed him?"" He said: ""The devils descended upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that night from the valleys and mountain passes, and among them was a devil holding a flame of fire in his hand, wanting to burn the face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Then Gabriel, peace be upon him, descended to him and said: 'O Muhammad! Say:' I said: 'And what should I say?' He said: 'Say: I seek refuge in the perfect words of Allah which neither the righteous nor the wicked can surpass, from the evil of what He created, scattered, and originated; and from the evil of what descends from the heaven and from the evil of what ascends therein; and from the evil of what He scattered in the earth and what emerges from it; and from the evil of the trials of the night and day; and from the evil of every visitor except a visitor who comes with good, O Most Merciful!' He said: So their fire was extinguished and Allah, Blessed and Exalted, defeated them."""""
