"2922","Anas ibn Malik reported: The Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to him and said: ""O Messenger of Allah! We are ruined, by the Lord of the Ka'ba!"" He said: ""And what is that?"" They said: ""Hypocrisy, hypocrisy!"" He said: ""Do you not testify that there is no deity but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah?"" They said: ""Yes, indeed."" He said: ""That is not hypocrisy."" Then they returned a second time and said: ""O Messenger of Allah! We are ruined, by the Lord of the Ka'ba!"" He said: ""And what is that?"" They said: ""Hypocrisy, hypocrisy!"" He said: ""Do you not testify that there is no deity but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah?"" They said: ""Yes, indeed."" He said: ""That is not hypocrisy."" Then they returned a third time and said the like of that, so he said to them: ""That is not hypocrisy."" They said: ""O Messenger of Allah! When we are with you, we are in a certain state, but when we leave your presence, worldly affairs and our families occupy us."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""If you were to remain, when you leave me, in the same state in which you are when you are with me, the angels would shake hands with you in the streets of Medina."""""
"2923","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 2923 Arabic Hadees: 2710"
"2924","Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī (may Allah be pleased with him) reported: The wife of Ṣafwān ibn al-Muʿaṭṭal came to the Prophet (ﷺ) while we were with him and said: ""O Messenger of Allah! My husband Ṣafwān ibn al-Muʿaṭṭal beats me when I pray, breaks my fast when I fast, and does not perform the Fajr prayer until the sun rises."" Ṣafwān was present with him. He asked him about what she had said. He replied: ""O Messenger of Allah! As for her saying that I beat her when she prays, she recites two sūrahs, so I forbade her from that."" He said: ""If it were a single sūrah, it would suffice the people."" ""As for her saying that I break her fast, she fasts while I am a young man and I cannot restrain myself."" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said on that day: ""A woman must not fast except with her husband's permission."" ""As for her saying that I do not pray until the sun rises, we are a household known for this; we hardly wake up until the sun rises."" He said: ""When you wake up, then pray."""""
"2925","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 2925 Arabic Hadees: 660"
"2926","On the authority of Abdullah ibn Shaddad, that a group of three men from Banu Udhra came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and accepted Islam. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Who will take care of them?"" Talha said: ""I will."" So they stayed with Talha. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent an expedition, and one of them went out in it and was martyred. Then he sent another expedition, and another of them went out in it and was martyred. Then the third died on his bed. Talha said: ""I saw these three who were with me in Paradise. I saw the one who died on his bed ahead of them, and I saw the one who was martyred last next to him, and I saw the one who was martyred first as the last of them."" He said: ""This caused me concern."" He said: ""So I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him."" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""What did you find objectionable about that? None is more excellent in the sight of Allah than a believer who is granted a long life in Islam for his glorification, magnification, and declaration of the oneness of Allah."""""
"2927","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 2927 Arabic Hadees: 555"
"2928","Abdullah ibn Mas'ud reported: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""No person is ever afflicted with anxiety and grief, and then says: 'O Allah, I am Your servant, son of Your servant, son of Your maidservant. My forelock is in Your hand, Your command over me is forever executed, and Your decree over me is just. I ask You by every name belonging to You which You have named Yourself with, or taught to any of Your creation, or revealed in Your Book, or preserved in the knowledge of the unseen with You, that You make the Quran the spring of my heart and the light of my chest, a departure for my sorrow and a release for my anxiety,' except that Allah will remove his anxiety and grief and replace them with relief."" It was said: ""O Messenger of Allah, should we not learn it?"" He said: ""Yes, whoever hears it should learn it."""""
