"2981","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 2981 Arabic Hadees: 2011"
"2982","On the authority of Thawbān, the freed slave of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who said: A Bedouin guest alighted with us. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sat before his dwellings and began asking him about the people: how was their joy in Islam, and how was their dedication to the prayer? He continued to inform him of that which pleased him until I saw the face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ become radiant.When midday arrived and it was time for the meal, he called me secretly, sparing no effort, saying: ""Go to ʿĀʾishah and inform her that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ has a guest."" She said: ""By Him Who sent him with guidance and the religion of truth, I have nothing in my hand this morning for anyone among the people to eat."" So he sent me back to his wives; all of them excused themselves with the same excuse ʿĀʾishah had given. I saw the complexion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ change (turn pale).The Bedouin said: ""We people of the desert are afflicted in our time; we are not people of the settled lands. A handful of dates, over which milk or water is drunk, constitutes abundance for us.""At that moment, a she-goat of ours passed by that had been milked; we used to call it ""Thumar Thumar."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called it by its name, ""Thumar Thumar,"" and it came to him humming. He took hold of its leg saying ""Bismillāh,"" then tethered it saying ""Bismillāh,"" then wiped its udder saying ""Bismillāh,"" whereupon it became full of milk.He called for a milking vessel; I brought it to him. He milked into it saying ""Bismillāh"" until he filled it. He handed it to the guest, who drank a large draught. When he wanted to set it down, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: ""Drink more (ʿUll)."" He wanted to set it down again, and he said to him: ""Drink more."" He kept repeating this to him until he had his fill and drank as much as Allah willed.Then he milked again saying ""Bismillāh"" and filled it, and said: ""Convey this to ʿĀʾishah."" She drank from it whatever she wished. Then I returned to him; he milked into it saying ""Bismillāh,"" then sent me with it to his wives. Whenever one of them drank from it, I returned it to him; he would milk again saying ""Bismillāh"" and fill it, until he said: ""Give it to the guest."" I gave it to him. He said: ""Bismillāh,"" and drank from it whatever Allah willed, then gave it to me. I could not refrain from placing my lips upon the spot of his lips, and I drank a drink sweeter than honey and more fragrant than musk.Then he said: ""O Allah, bless its people in it."""""
"2983","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 2983 Arabic Hadees: 3335"
"2984","Anas ibn Malik narrated from Ubayy ibn Ka'b who said: ""Nothing has troubled my mind since I embraced Islam except that I recited a verse and another person recited it differently from my recitation. I said: 'The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) taught me this verse.' And my companion said: 'The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) taught me this verse.' So we went to him and I said: 'O Messenger of Allah! Did you teach me such-and-such a verse?' He said: 'Yes.' And my companion said: 'Did you teach me such-and-such?' He said: 'Yes.' Gabriel and Michael came to me, so Gabriel sat on my right and Michael on my left. He said: 'Recite on one mode.' Michael said: 'Ask for more.' He said: 'Recite the Qur'an on two modes.' (He said: 'Ask for more') until it reached seven modes. (He said:) 'And each is sufficient and healing.'"""""
